Files, and why these ones
-------------------------

    netbird-systemtray-<state>.png            the coloured mark (256x256)
    netbird-systemtray-<state>-mono-dark.png  white silhouette (48x48)

for <state> in connected, connecting, disconnected, error, needs-login.

The upstream `-mono` variant is a black silhouette and `-mono-dark` is a white
one over the same alpha shape. Tinting preserves the source's luminance, so a
black source stays black whatever colour it is given; only the white
`-mono-dark` variant can carry an arbitrary theme colour, which is why it is
the one kept — despite the name it is not dark-theme-specific.

NOTE: the `-mono-dark` files are currently UNUSED. The widget ships colour
only. A themed monochrome style was built and withdrawn because the tint draws
nothing inside quickshell's layer-shell bar (it renders correctly under plain
`qml6`, and no error is logged either way). The files are kept, verified and
pinned so reviving that style is a code-only change.

At this commit netbird-systemtray-needs-login*.png is byte-identical to the
corresponding netbird-systemtray-error*.png. Both names are shipped so the
widget's state-to-file mapping stays a plain lookup.

